      "en": "Peptides having up to four amino acids in a fully defined sequence; Derivatives thereof; <br><br><b><u>Note(s)</u></b><br><br><ul><li>In this group, the following expression is used with the meaning indicated: <ul><li>\"first amino acid\" means the first amino acid from the left side, i.e. the N-terminal amino acid, of the peptide sequence. </li></ul></li></ul>",
